# SPA routing, for hosts that read a _redirects file
# (Cloudflare Pages / Workers static assets, Netlify, and the same syntax).
#
# The app is client-routed, so these paths must render index.html with a 200
# instead of a 404.
#
# They are listed explicitly rather than with a /* catch-all, on purpose:
# Cloudflare rejects "/* /index.html 200" as an infinite loop, because the
# destination /index.html matches that same rule again (Cloudflare's pretty-URL
# handling strips ".html", which re-triggers the rule).
#
# "/" needs no rule — it is served directly from index.html.
# Anything else falls through to 404.html, a copy of the app, and the router's
# catch-all route then sends the visitor to the home page.

/about      /index.html   200
/about20    /index.html   200
/home39     /index.html   200
